 :proposed-check
 {:name "bounded-writer wrap + deref/projection lint (write-size budget)"
  :how "Two layers. (1) Mechanical lint: flag every durable write sink — spit, Files/write, .write on a writer/channel, with-out-str pprint feeding a write — whose value expression is (a) a deref of an atom/var (@checkpoints, @phase-events), (b) a whole map threaded from a :judgment/:backtrace/:machine-state-bearing structure (track the key provenance the way we now know it flows: checkpoints -> backtrace -> finding -> brief-item/run-record/cohort-cell), or (c) a function parameter never passed through select-keys/update-in/elision before the write. Every hit must either route through a single approved bounded-writer wrapper or justify itself. (2) Runtime enforcement inside the wrapper: serialize to a byte array first, compare against a byte budget per record (e.g. 256 KB default), and on overflow refuse with a typed :durable-write-over-budget error carrying measured size and top-level key sizes — never silently truncate, because digest-verified immutables (realized_recording, run4 projections) must fail loudly rather than corrupt. Add a store-side invariant: after each publication, record the file size in the store index and refuse publication when a single record exceeds the budget or the store's total growth per click exceeds a ceiling. AMENDED (claude-4 review): the budget must distinguish record classes. For records re-read by code, refuse on overflow. For DIAGNOSTIC payloads (backtraces, witnesses) the budget governs representation, not retention — (a) serialise with pr-str, never pprint, under any lock (measured: one 19.4 MB finding went 47,306 ms -> 212 ms, 38% fewer bytes); (b) elide by reference, not deletion — write the judgment to a content-addressed blob and keep path+digest in the backtrace, the shape record-finding! already uses with {:trip-report path}. A refusal there would fail a click because its own post-mortem was too big, which is worse than the write cost."
  :false-positive-risk "(a) Legitimately large machine-round-trip stores (cohort cells, run records used for replay/digest verification) would be flagged — they need explicit budget exemptions, which is exactly the decision we want forced. (b) Key-provenance tracking over-approximates: a map that merely contains the key :judgment but holds a small scalar judgment (selection selected-mission) would cry wolf; the check should measure serialized size at the wrapper, not guess from key names alone — lint narrows the sites, runtime measurement decides. (c) pr-str-based stores already exist deliberately (full_loop_cohort comment 2026-07-25): the check must flag SIZE, not printer choice, or it re-litigates a settled decision."}}
